    "title": "Modesto police to hold DUI checkpoint - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Katie Chavez ,\n4 hours ago\n(FOX40.COM) — Police officers are cracking down on impaired drivers with a DUI checkpoint Friday in Modesto, officials said.\nVIDEO: Construction worker killed by suspected DUI driver on Highway 50 (August 2026)\nOfficers with the Modesto Police Department will conduct the checkpoint at an undisclosed location where there have been incidents of impaired driving-related crashes.\n\"Impaired drivers put others on the road at significant risk,\" said Darin Wilson, a traffic safety unit sergeant.\nAlcohol is not the only cause of driver impairment, the police department wrote in a social media post. Some prescription or over-the-counter drugs can do the trick, as well as marijuana.\nFirst-time DUI offenders face a suspended license and an average of $13,500 in fines and penalties, Modesto police said.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to FOX40 News.\n9",
    "summary": "(FOX40.COM) — Police officers are cracking down on impaired drivers with a DUI checkpoint Friday in Modesto, officials said. VIDEO: Construction worker killed by suspected DUI driver on Highway 50 (August 2026) Officers with the Modesto Police Department will conduct the checkpoint at an undisclosed location where there have been incidents of impaired driving-related crashes. \"Impaired drivers put others on the road at significant risk,\" said Darin Wilson, a traffic safety unit sergeant. Alcohol is not the only cause of driver impairment, the police department wrote in a social media post.",
